# Vercel CLI uploads the working tree when deploying without git, and when this
# file exists it is the ONLY ignore list consulted — .gitignore is not read.
# Everything the build does not need stays on this machine, and in particular
# infra/ (Terraform helpers and the gitignored secrets.auto.tfvars) is never
# part of a deployment's source bundle.
#
# Directory entries are ANCHORED to the repo root. A bare `supabase` matched
# src/lib/supabase/ as well and the first deploy failed with 94 "Module not
# found: @/lib/supabase/admin" errors.
node_modules
.next
.env
.env.*
.vercel
.claude
/infra
/docs
/design
/supabase
/scripts
/specs
/coverage
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.log
